// OAuth 2.0 login and token rotation for this CLI: the RFC 8628
// device grant, the API's browser approval (the API mints a key for
// this CLI behind a PKCE-shaped challenge), and refresh of a stored
// OAuth session. Everything runs on platform primitives because
// generated packages have no runtime dependencies. Login endpoints
// must be HTTPS (loopback HTTP is allowed for development), response
// bodies are size-bounded, redirects are never followed, and polling
// halts at the provider's own expiry.

